    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## Build a Bot That Actually Knows Something\r\n\r\nSomeone set up this bot to help new students — but they weren't careful about what information they gave it.\r\n\r\n##### Do This:\r\n\r\n1. Ask your bot a few questions a new student would ask. Something's off. What is it?\r\n2. Open the Retrieval Contexts panel. That's everything your bot knows. Read through it.\r\n3. Remove anything that shouldn't be there. Click Update, then ask your questions again.\r\n4. Try asking something your bot has no information about. What does it say now?\r\n\r\n##### Talk with your partner:\r\nCompare bots — did you remove the same things? Does having context mean the bot is always right?\r\n\r\n::: details [**Want to make it better?**]\r\nAdd any of these to your bot's context, then test whether it helps:\r\n\r\n- [Updated August 2026] The library is open until 5:00 pm on school days for homework help.\r\n- [Updated August 2026] Students who need a schedule change should see their counselor in Building A within the first two weeks.\r\n- [Updated August 2026] Bus routes and pickup zones are posted by the gym entrance each morning.\r\n\r\n:::\r\n\r\n::: details [**Ready for a challenge?**]\r\nWrite your own context entry about something a new student would want to know. Test whether your bot uses it.\r\n:::\r\n",
    "aichat_settings": {
